  "title": "Journal v2: schema-validated events, run index, and replay digest",
  "summary": "The journal grows from a two-payload buffer into a versioned, schema-validated event log. Events now carry a typed actor, work item, change and cost; every appended event is checked against a draft 2020-12 JSON schema before a byte is written, and a run-complete event must name the journal's current head. Journals move from `<state>/buffer` to `<state>/runs`, a per-work-item index under `<state>/index` records which runs belong to which work item under a file lock, and a reader replays a run end to end, verifying each link and computing a replay digest over decision fields only.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
